    "narrative": "Our offensive core for today is anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (79.25) and **Cal Raleigh** (74.89), who represent our clearest paths to production. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is an absolute must-start; despite a matchup against Barnett, his elite 19% SP skill bonus and high-leverage spot in the #2 hole make him our most efficient play. **Cal Raleigh** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor (+14%) and a soft matchup against Hughes, positioning him to provide the power ceiling we need. **Dylan Beavers** (67.10) also emerges as a high-value start in the leadoff spot; while he faces an \"Elite Hold\" pitcher, his +10% order bonus and +16% park adjustment offset the SB risk, making him a primary source of run-scoring potential today.\n\nWe are navigating several complex platoon and matchup variables, most notably with **Lawrence Butler** (52.29). While his platoon advantage is strong (+13%), he faces a formidable test against Espino (1.94 xERA), which suppresses his overall efficiency score. Conversely, **Daulton Varsho** (59.21) remains a recommended start because his platoon edge against Mahle is effectively maximized by his placement in the lineup. Our most difficult decision was keeping **Jung Hoo Lee** (44.57) on the bench; he was the primary candidate to displace **Alex Freeland** (47.52), but the optimizer ultimately stuck with **Alex Freeland** due to the higher consistency of the expected order spot and a favorable tilt against Perdomo. \n\nInvestors should monitor the status of **Will Smith** and **Alex Freeland**, as their scores are contingent on the \"Lineup Pending\" assumption remaining accurate; any drop in the batting order could trigger a re-evaluation of their utility. Furthermore, while **Lawrence Butler** carries a high platoon ceiling, the sheer skill level of Espino represents our highest risk of a sub-floor performance today. We are playing for efficiency while managing game caps, opting to leave players like **Zack Gelof** (39.57) and **Masyn Winn** (36.22) on the bench strictly to preserve their long-term value, as neither cleared our 40.0 baseline requirement for a daily start.",
